# Surgical React Version Synchronization

## Goal
Resolve the "Incompatible React versions" crash by unifying the entire monorepo on React 19.1.0, which is the version required by the Expo SDK 54 / React Native 0.81 renderer.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Why we need an override:**
> Even though we are using "in-built" packages, `@react-navigation` and other tools now have a peer dependency on React `^19.2.0`. However, the Native Renderer shipped inside Expo SDK 54 is strictly `19.1.0`. 
>
> To resolve this conflict, we must use a `pnpm.overrides` to force these libraries back to `19.1.0`. Without this, the app will continue to crash on launch.

## Proposed Changes

### [Monorepo Root]

#### [MODIFY] [package.json](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/package.json)
- Add `pnpm.overrides` to pin `react`, `react-dom`, and `@types/react` to `19.1.0`.
- Ensure `react-native-renderer` (if pulled separately) is also pinned.

### [gurudevi-mobile]

#### [MODIFY] [package.json](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/gurudevi-mobile/package.json)
- Ensure `react` is explicitly `19.1.0`.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- **Version Check**: Run `pnpm why react -r` to confirm NO version other than `19.1.0` exists in the tree.
- **BDD Harness**: Run `pnpm test` to ensure the testing tools (Jest 30, RNTL 14 Beta) still function with React 19.1.0.

### Manual Verification
- **App Launch**: Start the app with `npx expo start --clear` and verify the red screen error is gone.
- **Navigation Test**: Click through the app to ensure React Navigation works correctly with the forced 19.1.0 version.
